  "interpretation": [
    "The primary median is slightly slower and its interval includes parity while allowing more than 3% cost. No stable provisional regression is flagged; this does not establish equivalence or a speedup.",
    "Anonymous and wait4 peak memory decrease slightly with nominal intervals excluding parity; sampled post-exec VmHWM includes parity. These process peaks do not establish live JavaScript heap, allocation traffic, post-GC retention or an allocator size-class benefit.",
    "Exact-capacity object plus field storage grows 16 bytes for empty or larger objects, is equal for one field and saves 16 bytes for two fields. Actual Vec capacities and receiver populations matter; no allocation population or capacity census is available in this clean cohort.",
    "Clocks include compilation and rendering/collection work; they do not isolate compilation or natural GC. No optimizing-tier adoption claim follows from OPT_JIT=0.",
    "The seven-pair empirical bootstrap has small-sample limits. Primary sign bounds have at least 98.4375% median coverage under independent paired observations. Secondary intervals have no multiple-comparison correction. Every pair and tail is retained.",
    "No overall engine, Node/Ladybird, cross-host or client browser performance claim. Client validation remains separate if a later evidence-based representation change warrants it.",
    "Referenced raw artifacts and the experimental source patch are retained in ignored local investigation directories; they are not required build inputs or guaranteed in a fresh clone."
  ],
